{"title":"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 34","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_34\">Problem 34</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 34\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-inch and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-inch diameter poles are placed together and bound together with wire. \nThe length of the shortest wire that will go around them is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc208ab774b4965079ad4f83e09fc27f2a296d10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12\\sqrt{3}+16\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12\\sqrt{3}+7\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 12\\sqrt{3}+14\\pi\\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ 12+15\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 24\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"441\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d3da77c65cbd5a73905d6d85f447a910e1b9e84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),3)); draw(circle((12,0),9)); draw((-1,2sqrt(2)) -- (9,6sqrt(2))); draw((-1,-2sqrt(2)) -- (9,-6sqrt(2))); draw((0,0) -- (-1,2sqrt(2))); draw((12,0) -- (9,6sqrt(2))); draw((0,0) -- (12,0)); draw((0,0) -- (10,3sqrt(3))); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"188\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/512458e0a68b30de589536536637ac9c58e09f4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{A diagram of the problem...aside from a few blips.}\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"15\" />\nWe can separate the total length of the wire into two sections: the straight and the curve.\n</p><p>In order to find out the length of the straight, we can combine the two radii (halved because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are diameters) to be the hypotenuse and the difference between said radii to be the short leg. With this, we can establish a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle, which means that the remaining leg must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8772d61f5af0b70f355caf61084162db9b47f34b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> This is the length of one part of the straight. Since there are two parts, the total length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c1723df91fa4d618319811d633cbd6391341412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we find the curved part of the wire. We must first find the arc length of the curves, and the angle measurements to find the lengths. We can do this by doing two different things for two different circles. For the radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> circle, we can subtract two right angles and two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degree angles from the total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62a47cbc153efdf4611d8660429ea879be3f192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, which makes for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c230274ae221d6976c7fd22ed7f398e096e4ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360 - 240 = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"127\" height=\"13\" /> degree measure. That means that the curved section on the radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5b49047c6c0acaff8cade0d7192baf7b6bf96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}6\\pi=2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />. For the bigger circle, we can simply subtract twice the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degree angle from the circle to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/9/8a902a9b8174bbd2f86c913d42aeb9abef557d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360 - 120 = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"127\" height=\"13\" /> degrees. When plugged into the formula, then we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad417413dc187d779d43f601552bcfdbf6d1d52c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}18\\pi=12\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Add everything up and you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/72786b8bb99b12f9f7d6d5878360d0ed6e201d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 12\\sqrt{3} + 14\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"134\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to get back to the problem set, click <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems\">here</a>\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017161600\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.093 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 124/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 335/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4311/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.563      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n100.00%    5.563      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19535:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017161600 and revision id 131960. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}